# claude-quota-gauge config -- copy to ~/.claude/claude-quota-gauge.env and edit.
# All variables are optional; every one has a sane default. This file is loaded
# automatically by the scripts in bin/ (even when invoked from the statusline
# command, a SessionStart hook, or launchd, none of which inherit your shell
# profile's env vars).

# Path to your parked-issues file (see the PENDING.md convention in the README).
# Checked in this order if unset: ./PENDING.md (cwd), then ~/.claude/PENDING.md.
# CLAUDE_USAGE_PENDING_FILE=~/notes/PENDING.md

# Which model to show a separate calibrated weekly estimate for, beyond the
# two real rate_limits numbers -- only relevant if your account has its own
# weekly pool for one model (e.g. Fable) that Anthropic's rate_limits field
# doesn't break out. Matches by substring against model IDs in your local
# transcripts. Run /gauge-calibrate once after setting this.
# CLAUDE_USAGE_TRACK_MODEL=fable

# How many hours a calibration can go without re-verification before the
# tracked-model estimate reports itself stale (rather than a bare number).
# The estimate is projected from local Claude Code token usage only -- it
# can't see that model's usage through claude.ai web/mobile, so it silently
# falls behind reality if a meaningful share of usage happens off this CLI.
# Shorter = more frequent recalibration nudges, less time spent wrong.
#
# Since v0.10.0 this is only the BACKSTOP for usage the CLI can't observe at
# all (web/mobile) -- usage through this CLI itself is caught immediately by
# an event-driven trigger instead (an Agent-tool dispatch with model=<tracked
# model> marks it for recalibration on the very next prompt, no schedule
# involved). If most of your usage of the tracked model happens through this
# CLI, you can safely loosen this a lot (e.g. to a week) without losing much
# accuracy -- the event-driven path is doing the real work.
# CLAUDE_USAGE_FABLE_MAX_CAL_AGE_HOURS=12

# How many percentage points of UNEXPLAINED aggregate-weekly movement (the
# real aggregate % from rate_limits moving beyond what local usage since the
# last calibration accounts for) trip the tracked-model estimate to stale
# immediately, rather than waiting for CLAUDE_USAGE_FABLE_MAX_CAL_AGE_HOURS
# to elapse. Locally-explained movement is subtracted out first, so this can
# sit tight without false alarms on heavy CLI days. Same v0.10.0 note as
# above applies -- this is a backstop, not the primary trigger anymore.
# CLAUDE_USAGE_FABLE_DRIFT_THRESHOLD=2

# Desktop-notification threshold for the background watcher (usage-watch.py).
# CLAUDE_USAGE_ALERT_THRESHOLD=85

# macOS-only: flags in the background (via the UserPromptSubmit hook, never
# the visible statusline bar) when the OS light/dark appearance has drifted
# from what a session's UI theme actually resolved against at launch --
# Claude Code checks that once at startup and never again, so a long-open
# session's colors silently go stale with `/config theme=auto` as the only
# fix. Off by default everywhere since it's a platform-specific add-on.
# CLAUDE_USAGE_THEME_WATCH=1
